1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,747
Sweetheart, there's no supper in the world

2
00:00:02,747 --> 00:00:05,036
that says somebody loves you like a

3
00:00:05,036 --> 00:00:06,083
chicken pot pie.

4
00:00:06,263 --> 00:00:07,954
A golden, flaky crust,

5
00:00:07,954 --> 00:00:10,028
and when you break into it,

6
00:00:10,028 --> 00:00:11,565
the steam rolls out,

7
00:00:11,565 --> 00:00:15,254
and underneath there's chicken and vegetables in

8
00:00:15,254 --> 00:00:16,944
a thick, creamy gravy.

9
00:00:17,124 --> 00:00:19,927
When my husband had his gallbladder out

10
00:00:19,927 --> 00:00:21,724
in nineteen seventy-nine,

11
00:00:21,724 --> 00:00:24,311
the whole church brought casseroles.

12
00:00:24,491 --> 00:00:25,756
Mrs.

13
00:00:25,936 --> 00:00:28,131
Hartman brought a pot pie.

14
00:00:28,311 --> 00:00:29,320
He married me,

15
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,196
but I think he loved her a

16
00:00:31,196 --> 00:00:31,701
little.

17
00:00:32,051 --> 00:00:34,787
But people tell me their pot pie

18
00:00:34,787 --> 00:00:35,813
has a soggy,

19
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:37,438
gummy bottom crust,

20
00:00:37,438 --> 00:00:40,004
or the filling runs like soup,

21
00:00:40,004 --> 00:00:41,629
or it tastes bland.

22
00:00:41,809 --> 00:00:44,569
So tonight I'm giving you my chicken

23
00:00:44,569 --> 00:00:46,103
pot pie, every step,

24
00:00:46,103 --> 00:00:48,709
and the five mistakes that make it

25
00:00:48,709 --> 00:00:49,169
soggy.

26
00:00:49,349 --> 00:00:50,541
And stay with me,

27
00:00:50,541 --> 00:00:52,854
because the last trick is for the

28
00:00:52,854 --> 00:00:55,306
bottom crust, and it's the one that

29
00:00:55,306 --> 00:00:57,059
makes all the difference.

30
00:00:57,409 --> 00:00:58,895
In the old days,

31
00:00:58,895 --> 00:01:02,703
honey, chicken pot pie wasn't fancy food.

32
00:01:02,883 --> 00:01:05,050
It was what you made on Monday

33
00:01:05,050 --> 00:01:07,434
with the leftover Sunday chicken.

34
00:01:07,614 --> 00:01:10,229
Every bit of meat picked off the

35
00:01:10,229 --> 00:01:12,355
bones, the leftover gravy,

36
00:01:12,355 --> 00:01:14,153
some carrots and peas,

37
00:01:14,153 --> 00:01:15,706
and a crust on top.

38
00:01:15,886 --> 00:01:17,244
Nothing wasted.

39
00:01:17,424 --> 00:01:20,030
Grandma Pearl made hers in a big

40
00:01:20,030 --> 00:01:21,495
cast iron skillet,

41
00:01:21,495 --> 00:01:23,694
and it fed eight farmhands.

42
00:01:24,044 --> 00:01:26,340
Then in the nineteen fifties,

43
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:28,716
the frozen pot pie came along,

44
00:01:28,716 --> 00:01:31,330
the little ones in the foil tins,

45
00:01:31,330 --> 00:01:32,914
nineteen cents each.

46
00:01:33,094 --> 00:01:35,693
My brother Danny thought they were the

47
00:01:35,693 --> 00:01:38,156
most wonderful invention in history.

48
00:01:38,336 --> 00:01:40,739
My mother thought they were an insult.

49
00:01:40,919 --> 00:01:42,331
She'd say, Danny,

50
00:01:42,331 --> 00:01:44,075
that's not a pot pie,

51
00:01:44,075 --> 00:01:45,737
that's a punishment.

52
00:01:45,917 --> 00:01:47,374
He ate them anyway,

53
00:01:47,374 --> 00:01:50,365
standing up, every Saturday she went to

54
00:01:50,365 --> 00:01:51,362
her sister's.

55
00:01:51,712 --> 00:01:54,308
And today, a homemade pot pie feeds

56
00:01:54,308 --> 00:01:56,978
six people for about twelve dollars,

57
00:01:56,978 --> 00:01:59,055
and it's the best way I know

58
00:01:59,055 --> 00:02:01,726
to use a rotisserie chicken from the

59
00:02:01,726 --> 00:02:02,764
grocery store.

60
00:02:02,944 --> 00:02:04,872
In a minute I'll tell you how

61
00:02:04,872 --> 00:02:06,800
to make the whole thing in an

62
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,928
hour, with a store-bought crust,

63
00:02:08,928 --> 00:02:11,122
and nobody at the table will ever

64
00:02:11,122 --> 00:02:11,454
know.

65
00:02:11,805 --> 00:02:13,683
Here's what you need,

66
00:02:13,683 --> 00:02:14,219
honey.

67
00:02:14,399 --> 00:02:16,584
Three cups of cooked chicken,

68
00:02:16,584 --> 00:02:17,940
shredded or cubed.

69
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:21,018
A rotisserie chicken gives you just about

70
00:02:21,018 --> 00:02:21,371
that.

71
00:02:21,551 --> 00:02:23,920
Six tablespoons of butter.

72
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,972
One onion, two carrots and two ribs

73
00:02:26,972 --> 00:02:28,860
of celery, all chopped.

74
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:31,234
A third of a cup of flour.

75
00:02:31,414 --> 00:02:33,388
Two cups of chicken broth.

76
00:02:33,568 --> 00:02:35,880
One cup of milk or half and

77
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:36,308
half.

78
00:02:36,488 --> 00:02:38,647
One cup of frozen peas.

79
00:02:38,827 --> 00:02:40,535
Fresh thyme, salt,

80
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:41,579
and pepper.

81
00:02:41,929 --> 00:02:43,217
And the crust.

82
00:02:43,397 --> 00:02:45,860
Two crusts for a nine-inch deep dish

83
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:47,980
pie pan, one for the bottom and

84
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:49,075
one for the top.

85
00:02:49,255 --> 00:02:50,943
You can make your own,

86
00:02:50,943 --> 00:02:54,165
or use the refrigerated rolled crusts from

87
00:02:54,165 --> 00:02:56,544
the store, and that's what I do

88
00:02:56,544 --> 00:02:57,695
on a weeknight.

89
00:02:57,875 --> 00:02:58,818
And one egg,

90
00:02:58,818 --> 00:03:01,096
beaten with a spoon of water,

91
00:03:01,096 --> 00:03:03,611
for brushing the top so it turns

92
00:03:03,611 --> 00:03:05,654
that beautiful shiny gold.

93
00:03:06,004 --> 00:03:08,203
And if you want to make your

94
00:03:08,203 --> 00:03:09,538
own crust, honey,

95
00:03:09,538 --> 00:03:11,344
here's Grandma Pearl's.

96
00:03:11,524 --> 00:03:13,886
Two and a half cups of flour,

97
00:03:13,886 --> 00:03:15,434
a teaspoon of salt,

98
00:03:15,434 --> 00:03:17,796
a cup of very cold butter cut

99
00:03:17,796 --> 00:03:19,099
in small pieces,

100
00:03:19,099 --> 00:03:21,299
and about half a cup of ice

101
00:03:21,299 --> 00:03:21,787
water.

102
00:03:21,967 --> 00:03:24,249
Rub the butter into the flour with

103
00:03:24,249 --> 00:03:27,000
your fingertips until it looks like small

104
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,081
peas, add the water a little at

105
00:03:29,081 --> 00:03:31,027
a time, and press it into two

106
00:03:31,027 --> 00:03:31,429
discs.

107
00:03:31,609 --> 00:03:33,142
Chill them an hour.

108
00:03:33,322 --> 00:03:36,062
Cold butter is what makes it flaky.

109
00:03:36,412 --> 00:03:37,352
Step one.

110
00:03:37,532 --> 00:03:39,814
Melt the butter in a big skillet

111
00:03:39,814 --> 00:03:41,027
over medium heat.

112
00:03:41,207 --> 00:03:42,207
Add the onion,

113
00:03:42,207 --> 00:03:43,565
carrots and celery,

114
00:03:43,565 --> 00:03:45,851
and cook them for about eight to

115
00:03:45,851 --> 00:03:48,138
ten minutes, until they're soft.

116
00:03:48,318 --> 00:03:51,819
Mistake number one is putting raw vegetables

117
00:03:51,819 --> 00:03:52,695
in the pie.

118
00:03:52,875 --> 00:03:55,533
The pie only bakes about forty minutes,

119
00:03:55,533 --> 00:03:58,122
and the carrots stay hard and crunchy.

120
00:03:58,302 --> 00:03:59,669
Cook them first,

121
00:03:59,669 --> 00:04:02,488
until a fork slides into a carrot

122
00:04:02,488 --> 00:04:03,086
easily.

123
00:04:03,436 --> 00:04:06,742
Now sprinkle the flour over the vegetables,

124
00:04:06,742 --> 00:04:08,665
and stir for two minutes,

125
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:11,203
so the raw flour taste cooks out.

126
00:04:11,383 --> 00:04:13,584
Then slowly pour in the broth,

127
00:04:13,584 --> 00:04:15,344
stirring the whole time,

128
00:04:15,344 --> 00:04:16,665
and then the milk.

129
00:04:16,845 --> 00:04:19,062
Bring it to a simmer and let

130
00:04:19,062 --> 00:04:21,753
it bubble gently for three or four

131
00:04:21,753 --> 00:04:23,811
minutes, until it's thick,

132
00:04:23,811 --> 00:04:24,682
like gravy.

133
00:04:24,862 --> 00:04:26,688
It should coat the back of a

134
00:04:26,688 --> 00:04:27,079
spoon.

135
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:29,949
And here's mistake number two.

136
00:04:30,129 --> 00:04:31,545
A thin filling.

137
00:04:31,725 --> 00:04:33,937
If the filling is runny when it

138
00:04:33,937 --> 00:04:36,077
goes in, it'll be soup when it

139
00:04:36,077 --> 00:04:38,860
comes out, and it'll soak right through

140
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:40,073
the bottom crust.

141
00:04:40,253 --> 00:04:42,041
Make it thicker than you think.

142
00:04:42,221 --> 00:04:44,459
It loosens up a little in the

143
00:04:44,459 --> 00:04:44,845
oven.

144
00:04:45,025 --> 00:04:46,226
If it's too thin,

145
00:04:46,226 --> 00:04:48,276
simmer it a few minutes more,

146
00:04:48,276 --> 00:04:50,184
or stir in a spoon of flour

147
00:04:50,184 --> 00:04:52,304
mixed with a little cold milk.

148
00:04:52,655 --> 00:04:54,378
If this is helping you,

149
00:04:54,378 --> 00:04:56,927
honey, tap the like button for me.

150
00:04:57,107 --> 00:04:59,940
It helps Grandma more than you know.

151
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:02,012
Now stir in the chicken,

152
00:05:02,012 --> 00:05:03,274
the frozen peas,

153
00:05:03,274 --> 00:05:06,192
and a teaspoon of fresh thyme leaves.

154
00:05:06,372 --> 00:05:07,602
And taste it.

155
00:05:07,782 --> 00:05:10,848
Mistake number three is a bland filling.

156
00:05:11,028 --> 00:05:13,730
It needs plenty of salt and pepper,

157
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:15,429
more than you'd think,

158
00:05:15,429 --> 00:05:17,436
because the crust is mild.

159
00:05:17,616 --> 00:05:20,437
Grandma Pearl added a pinch of nutmeg

160
00:05:20,437 --> 00:05:22,191
and a splash of sherry.

161
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:24,790
So far, cooked vegetables,

162
00:05:24,790 --> 00:05:26,002
a thick gravy,

163
00:05:26,002 --> 00:05:28,078
and plenty of seasoning.

164
00:05:28,258 --> 00:05:30,285
Now, mistake number four,

165
00:05:30,285 --> 00:05:32,717
and this one surprises people.

166
00:05:32,897 --> 00:05:35,335
Putting the hot filling into the crust.

167
00:05:35,515 --> 00:05:37,851
Hot filling melts the butter in the

168
00:05:37,851 --> 00:05:39,988
crust before it ever gets to the

169
00:05:39,988 --> 00:05:42,191
oven, and the bottom turns gummy.

170
00:05:42,371 --> 00:05:44,592
Let the filling cool for at least

171
00:05:44,592 --> 00:05:46,274
twenty to thirty minutes,

172
00:05:46,274 --> 00:05:47,688
until it's just warm.

173
00:05:47,868 --> 00:05:49,830
Or make it the day before.

174
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:52,716
And this is where the hour comes

175
00:05:52,716 --> 00:05:54,301
in, like I promised.

176
00:05:54,481 --> 00:05:55,883
Make the filling,

177
00:05:55,883 --> 00:05:57,450
and while it cools,

178
00:05:57,450 --> 00:06:00,172
take the crusts out of the icebox

179
00:06:00,172 --> 00:06:01,656
and heat the oven.

180
00:06:01,836 --> 00:06:03,510
Thirty minutes of work,

181
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:05,767
then forty minutes in the oven,

182
00:06:05,767 --> 00:06:08,096
while you set the table and help

183
00:06:08,096 --> 00:06:09,115
with homework.

184
00:06:09,295 --> 00:06:10,648
On a busy Tuesday,

185
00:06:10,648 --> 00:06:13,653
that's a real home-cooked supper with no

186
00:06:13,653 --> 00:06:14,555
fuss at all.

187
00:06:14,904 --> 00:06:17,167
And now the trick I promised,

188
00:06:17,167 --> 00:06:18,805
for the bottom crust.

189
00:06:18,985 --> 00:06:21,268
Mistake number five is putting a raw

190
00:06:21,268 --> 00:06:23,170
bottom crust in a glass pan in

191
00:06:23,170 --> 00:06:24,628
the middle of the oven.

192
00:06:24,808 --> 00:06:27,133
The bottom never gets hot enough to

193
00:06:27,133 --> 00:06:29,591
crisp up before the filling soaks in.

194
00:06:29,771 --> 00:06:31,130
Here's the fix.

195
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:33,445
Put a baking sheet on the lowest

196
00:06:33,445 --> 00:06:34,579
rack of the oven,

197
00:06:34,579 --> 00:06:36,780
and heat the oven to four hundred

198
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:39,583
twenty-five, with the baking sheet inside,

199
00:06:39,583 --> 00:06:41,317
for a good twenty minutes.

200
00:06:41,667 --> 00:06:44,211
Then fit the bottom crust into your

201
00:06:44,211 --> 00:06:46,683
pie pan, and brush the inside with

202
00:06:46,683 --> 00:06:48,645
a little of the beaten egg.

203
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:50,709
That egg makes a thin seal,

204
00:06:50,709 --> 00:06:51,826
like a raincoat,

205
00:06:51,826 --> 00:06:54,478
that keeps the gravy from soaking into

206
00:06:54,478 --> 00:06:55,176
the crust.

207
00:06:55,356 --> 00:06:57,794
Then pour in the cooled filling.

208
00:06:57,974 --> 00:06:59,906
Put the pie pan right on that

209
00:06:59,906 --> 00:07:01,039
hot baking sheet.

210
00:07:01,219 --> 00:07:04,123
The heat from below cooks the bottom

211
00:07:04,123 --> 00:07:05,816
crust fast and crisp,

212
00:07:05,816 --> 00:07:07,349
like a pizza stone.

213
00:07:07,699 --> 00:07:09,938
And use a metal pie pan if

214
00:07:09,938 --> 00:07:11,057
you have one,

215
00:07:11,057 --> 00:07:13,469
honey, not glass or ceramic.

216
00:07:13,649 --> 00:07:16,357
Metal gets hot faster and crisps the

217
00:07:16,357 --> 00:07:17,410
bottom better.

218
00:07:17,590 --> 00:07:18,839
Glass is pretty,

219
00:07:18,839 --> 00:07:20,869
and it lets you see if the

220
00:07:20,869 --> 00:07:22,118
bottom is brown.

221
00:07:22,298 --> 00:07:23,764
If you use glass,

222
00:07:23,764 --> 00:07:25,920
give it ten more minutes.

223
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:29,349
Grandma Pearl used her cast iron skillet,

224
00:07:29,349 --> 00:07:32,202
and her bottom crust was never soggy

225
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:33,786
once in fifty years.

226
00:07:34,137 --> 00:07:36,336
Now lay the top crust over the

227
00:07:36,336 --> 00:07:36,923
filling.

228
00:07:37,103 --> 00:07:38,144
Trim the edges,

229
00:07:38,144 --> 00:07:40,573
leaving about an inch hanging over,

230
00:07:40,573 --> 00:07:43,003
and fold it under the bottom crust,

231
00:07:43,003 --> 00:07:45,363
then crimp it with your fingers or

232
00:07:45,363 --> 00:07:46,820
press it with a fork.

233
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,230
Cut four or five slits in the

234
00:07:49,230 --> 00:07:51,459
top, so the steam can escape.

235
00:07:51,639 --> 00:07:54,098
Brush the whole top with the beaten

236
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:54,379
egg.

237
00:07:54,559 --> 00:07:57,345
Sprinkle a little coarse salt and pepper

238
00:07:57,345 --> 00:07:57,833
on top.

239
00:07:58,182 --> 00:08:00,288
Bake it on the hot baking sheet

240
00:08:00,288 --> 00:08:03,345
at four twenty-five for about twenty minutes,

241
00:08:03,345 --> 00:08:06,062
then turn it down to three seventy-five,

242
00:08:06,062 --> 00:08:08,847
and bake it another twenty to twenty-five

243
00:08:08,847 --> 00:08:11,360
minutes, until the top is deep golden

244
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:13,806
brown and the filling is bubbling up

245
00:08:13,806 --> 00:08:15,029
through the slits.

246
00:08:15,209 --> 00:08:17,333
If the edges get too brown,

247
00:08:17,333 --> 00:08:19,771
cover them with strips of foil.

248
00:08:19,951 --> 00:08:22,941
Then let it rest fifteen minutes before

249
00:08:22,941 --> 00:08:25,164
cutting, so the filling sets.

250
00:08:25,515 --> 00:08:26,849
Serve it simple,

251
00:08:26,849 --> 00:08:27,767
sweetheart.

252
00:08:27,947 --> 00:08:30,287
A big spoonful on each plate,

253
00:08:30,287 --> 00:08:33,193
with a green salad or some cranberry

254
00:08:33,193 --> 00:08:34,646
sauce on the side.

255
00:08:34,826 --> 00:08:36,556
That's all it needs.

256
00:08:36,736 --> 00:08:39,557
My husband liked a slice of sharp

257
00:08:39,557 --> 00:08:40,839
cheddar on top,

258
00:08:40,839 --> 00:08:41,438
melted.

259
00:08:41,618 --> 00:08:44,704
And the leftovers are wonderful for lunch

260
00:08:44,704 --> 00:08:45,682
the next day,

261
00:08:45,682 --> 00:08:47,112
warmed in the oven,

262
00:08:47,112 --> 00:08:48,467
not the microwave,

263
00:08:48,467 --> 00:08:50,348
so the crust stays crisp.

264
00:08:50,699 --> 00:08:53,455
You can make this with leftover turkey

265
00:08:53,455 --> 00:08:55,340
after Thanksgiving, honey,

266
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:56,863
and it's even better.

267
00:08:57,043 --> 00:08:59,462
Or use a puff pastry sheet on

268
00:08:59,462 --> 00:09:01,547
top instead of pie crust,

269
00:09:01,547 --> 00:09:02,548
for a flaky,

270
00:09:02,548 --> 00:09:03,382
fancy top.

271
00:09:03,562 --> 00:09:06,154
Or skip the crust altogether and drop

272
00:09:06,154 --> 00:09:08,466
biscuits on top of the filling in

273
00:09:08,466 --> 00:09:09,867
a cast iron skillet.

274
00:09:10,047 --> 00:09:12,891
My granddaughter makes little pot pies in

275
00:09:12,891 --> 00:09:15,875
muffin tins for her children's lunch boxes.

276
00:09:16,224 --> 00:09:18,138
And it freezes beautifully,

277
00:09:18,138 --> 00:09:18,918
sweetheart.

278
00:09:19,098 --> 00:09:20,699
Make two, bake one,

279
00:09:20,699 --> 00:09:22,637
and freeze one unbaked,

280
00:09:22,637 --> 00:09:25,502
wrapped tight in plastic and foil,

281
00:09:25,502 --> 00:09:26,935
for three months.

282
00:09:27,115 --> 00:09:29,578
Bake it straight from frozen at four

283
00:09:29,578 --> 00:09:31,767
hundred, for about an hour and a

284
00:09:31,767 --> 00:09:34,024
quarter, with foil on top for the

285
00:09:34,024 --> 00:09:35,393
first forty minutes.

286
00:09:35,573 --> 00:09:38,192
When a neighbor is sick or has

287
00:09:38,192 --> 00:09:39,152
a new baby,

288
00:09:39,152 --> 00:09:41,683
I take them a frozen pot pie,

289
00:09:41,683 --> 00:09:42,469
like Mrs.

290
00:09:42,649 --> 00:09:44,019
Hartman did.

291
00:09:44,368 --> 00:09:45,750
So one more time.

292
00:09:45,930 --> 00:09:48,090
Cook the vegetables first.

293
00:09:48,270 --> 00:09:49,907
Make the gravy thick.

294
00:09:50,087 --> 00:09:51,355
Season it well,

295
00:09:51,355 --> 00:09:52,455
and taste it.

296
00:09:52,635 --> 00:09:54,342
Let the filling cool.

297
00:09:54,522 --> 00:09:56,861
A hot baking sheet on the lowest

298
00:09:56,861 --> 00:09:57,227
rack.

299
00:09:57,407 --> 00:10:00,253
Egg wash inside the bottom crust,

300
00:10:00,253 --> 00:10:01,633
like a raincoat.

301
00:10:01,813 --> 00:10:02,781
Slits on top,

302
00:10:02,781 --> 00:10:05,240
and bake it until it's golden and

303
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:05,911
bubbling.

304
00:10:06,091 --> 00:10:07,833
Rest fifteen minutes.

305
00:10:08,013 --> 00:10:10,323
That's a chicken pot pie with a

306
00:10:10,323 --> 00:10:12,111
crisp bottom every time.

307
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:14,443
Tell me in the comments,

308
00:10:14,443 --> 00:10:15,351
sweetheart.

309
00:10:15,531 --> 00:10:18,630
Homemade pot pie or the little frozen

310
00:10:18,630 --> 00:10:19,049
ones?

311
00:10:19,229 --> 00:10:22,445
Be honest, I won't tell your grandmother.

312
00:10:22,625 --> 00:10:25,740
The whole playlist of Grandma's recipes is

313
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:27,743
right there on your screen,

314
00:10:27,743 --> 00:10:29,820
and I'll see you in the next

315
00:10:29,820 --> 00:10:30,265
video.

316
00:10:30,445 --> 00:10:32,012
Good night, honey.
